.TH CAWGET-CLI 1 "2026" "cawget-cli 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cawget-cli \- command line of the Cawget segmented HTTP/HTTPS download manager
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cawget-cli
[\-\-db FILE] COMMAND [OPTIONS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Splits downloads into byte ranges fetched over parallel HTTP/HTTPS connections, resumes interrupted downloads, and keeps a persistent queue in SQLite. Only one scheduler (cawget-cli run, or the Cawget app) works on a database at a time; add, pause, resume, rm and list work while it runs.
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B get [opts] URL
Queue URL and download it immediately.
.TP
.B add [opts] URL...
Queue downloads without starting them.
.TP
.B run [\-j N] [\-l RATE] [\-\-daemon] [\-q]
Process the queue.
.TP
.B list, status ID
Show jobs.
.TP
.B pause ID, resume ID, rm [\-\-files] ID, clean
Manage jobs.
.TP
.B config [KEY [VALUE]] [\-\-unset]
Show or change settings (segments, max_jobs, min_segment_size, max_speed, retries, connect_timeout, cacert, user_agent, download_dir, window).
.SH OPTIONS (add, get)
.TP
.B \-o FILE, \-d DIR
Output file or directory.
.TP
.B \-s N
Connections per file (1\-64).
.TP
.B \-H "Name: value", \-\-referer URL, \-\-cookie STR, \-A AGENT
Request headers.
.TP
.B \-\-sha256 HEX
Verify the completed file.
.TP
.B \-\-at WHEN
Start later: +10m, +2h, HH:MM, "YYYY\-MM\-DD HH:MM", @epoch.
.SH FILES
.I $XDG_DATA_HOME/cawget/cawget.db
(default ~/.local/share/cawget/cawget.db; override with --db or CAWGET_DB). The directory is created 0700
and the database 0600. Credentials (logins, proxy logins, cookies, custom headers) are stored in the system
keyring (Secret Service), not in the database, which keeps only a reference. On first use after an upgrade,
plaintext credentials from an older database are migrated to the keyring: the database is backed up next to it
(cawget.db.pre-keyring-<timestamp>.bak), each login is written and verified in the keyring, then the plaintext is
cleared; without a keyring the migration is postponed and the plaintext stays.
On first use, if it does not exist, the first legacy database found is copied there, in this order:
~/.local/share/jackdaw/jackdaw.db, then
~/.local/share/segget/segget.db.
The old file is never changed.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CAWGET_DB
Database file, unless --db is given.
.TP
.B JACKDAW_DB, SEGGET_DB
Deprecated aliases of CAWGET_DB (JACKDAW_DB wins over SEGGET_DB); a note is printed when one is used.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 success, 1 a job failed, 130 interrupted (progress saved), 2 usage error.
